sequenceDiagram
  %% Nick 2026-11-06: a task VM never holds a GitHub credential, and the step mints its token when it runs, not at admission.
  %% Target design: stage 4 of the command development pipeline (docs/reference/pipeline/4-pr-and-ci.mmd, "Admit the merge step"), R2-R3. The Gateway admits and names the vault key, the step mints its token, and Swamp calls GitHub. docs/reference/tasks.md#ready-and-merge-a-task-pull-request.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · API / MCP (task-pr-merge)
  %% kind: tasks.pr_merge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as API / MCP<br/>typed API request
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  CLI->>GW: Merge the PR of GROUP<br/>head SHA
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `POST /api/v1/tasks/GROUP/pr-merge` with `head_sha` and an `Idempotency-Key`
  %%> - syntax: the MCP tool `task-pr-merge` with `group`, `head_sha`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - a Node with an access grant to the Gateway; there is no `orbit` command
  GW->>GH: Read the PR reviews<br/>short poll · approval on head
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the PR, its reviews and the check runs of the head with read-only App tokens (`pull_requests: read`, `checks: read`)
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the Gateway is private and its App receives no webhooks, so a caller that polls this command sees the approval
  GH-->>GW: Approval on the head
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the reviewer's latest decision is an approval of exactly this head; a later push moves the head and voids it
  Note over GW: Check the gate<br/>approval · CI green · key name
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the tasks extension is on, and the group is an open external group with a published PR that is open and no longer a draft
  %%> - the PR head is exactly `head_sha`, and the Project's merge check (`Required checks`) passed on that head
  %%> - the gate holds: the configured reviewer's latest review is an approval on this exact head (manual mode); a missing approval, a request for changes or a moved head refuses with its own code
  %%> - no other task runs on the group; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - names the vault key `pr-merge-write-<uuid>` for the write token; it mints no token
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a token lives one hour and an approval can take longer, so the merge step mints its own token when it runs
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - the automatic gate, a fresh self-review agent with at most 3 rounds; the approval is the only gate
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-pr-merge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); no Node is a target
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the repository, PR number and expected head
  %%> - the vault key name of the token, never the token
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task id
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the caller follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>GW: Mint the token<br/>operation:direct:github-token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the first step posts the run id to the Gateway; the Gateway checks the Operation, the run and the repository, mints a token with only `contents: write` and `pull_requests: write`, and writes it to the vault key that admission named
  %%> Why here and not at admission:
  %%> - an installation token lives one hour; the token is minted when the step that uses it runs
  %%> - no task VM holds a GitHub credential
  SW->>GH: Squash on expected head
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one squash merge straight into the base branch, with the admitted `sha`; a moved head refuses without merging
  %%> - no read of the PR comes first: admission read the head, and the `sha` of the call is the guard for the seconds in between
  %%> - no merge queue and no GitHub auto-merge
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a conflict with the base branch; the author rebases, which reruns CI and the proof, and the gate starts again
  SW->>GH: Clean up the token<br/>task-github-cleanup
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the shared cleanup child: it revokes the token, best effort because the token expires within one hour, and removes the private GitHub CLI configuration directory of this run
  %%> When:
  %%> - always, on success and failure
  Note over SW: Confirm the merge
  alt merged
    GH-->>SW: PR merged · sha
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the merge commit SHA
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · merge sha
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the merge<br/>task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task succeeds with the merge SHA; CI then runs on the new base commit, and nothing is deployed here
  else refused or failed
    GH--xSW: head moved or conflict
    %%> When:
    %%> - the head moved, the PR conflicts with the base branch, or GitHub refused the merge
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, such as `tasks_pr.merge_refused`
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>PR open · author fixes
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task fails; the PR stays open, unmerged
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - a new request for the same head is a new task with a new token; the gate is read again
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
